{"availability":"available","full":"brianmojena/al-dia-pos","name":"al-dia-pos","description":"POS e inventario para MIPYMES cubanas — React + Express serverless + Turso, con app de escritorio offline-first en Electron (outbox transaccional)","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-07T17:12:21Z","updated":"2026-10-12T00:46:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://al-dia-pos.vercel.app","topics":["cuba","electron","express","inventory-management","libsql","multi-tenant","offline-first","pos","react","serverless","turso","vercel"],"demo":"https://client-tan-one-13.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.499Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.499Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.499Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.499Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A point-of-sale and inventory system built for Cuban small businesses (MIPYMES), where intermittent internet is the norm, not the exception. One backend, three clients: a web app, an offline-first desktop app, and a native mobile dashboard for the business owner.","🇪🇸 Léeme en español · 🖥️ Live demo · 📱 Owner dashboard (separate repo)","Cuban MIPYMES run on cash boxes and paper notebooks. The off-the-shelf POS options assume things that don't hold in Cuba: a stable connection, card terminals, a stock catalogue in USD, an app store account. This system starts from the opposite assumptions:"],"features":["Point of sale — search-as-you-type, cart, checkout in one tap, cash or transfer. A persistent bar shows the owner-set transfer ceiling and USD rate; transfers over the ceiling are blocked, not merely warned about.","Inventory — create/edit/delete products with purchase price, sale price and stock. Margin is derived, not stored, so historical sales keep the cost that applied at the time.","Dashboard — today's revenue, estimated profit, sale count, low-stock alerts.","Sales history — grouped by day, expandable to line items.","Accounts & plans — registration, login, and two plans: Premium ($5 USD/month, simulated — there is no payment processor wired up) and Plan Dev (free, used for prototyping)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5e211a96702722f8808193ac439b765fccdf1d39532dcdbb201c5d3a68534dda","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.643Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.643Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A point-of-sale and inventory system built for Cuban small businesses (MIPYMES), where intermittent internet is the norm, not the exception. One backend, three clients: a web app, an offline-first desktop app, and a native mobile dashboard for the business owner.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"A point-of-sale and inventory system built for Cuban small businesses (MIPYMES), where intermittent internet is the norm, not the exception. One backend, three clients: a web app, an offline-first desktop app, and a native mobile dashboard for the business owner.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Accounts & plans — registration, login, and two plans: Premium ($5 USD/month, simulated — there is no payment processor wired up) and Plan Dev (free, used for prototyping).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5e211a96702722f8808193ac439b765fccdf1d39532dcdbb201c5d3a68534dda","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:35.643Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T00:46:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianmojena/al-dia-pos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:5